---
export const title = 'Forms and states';
export const order = 200;
import DemoComponentCard from '../../../../components/DemoComponentCard.astro';
---

<p>
  The pad is form-associated. Inside a <code>&lt;form&gt;</code> the signature is submitted under
  <code>name</code> as a PNG file (<code>&lt;name&gt;.png</code>), like a file input, so the server
  receives an ordinary upload instead of a base64 string a third larger.
  <code>required</code> blocks submission until the person signs, and <code>form.reset()</code>
  clears the pad. <code>readonly</code> shows the signature without the buttons;
  <code>disabled</code> also dims it.
</p>

<DemoComponentCard lang={'html'}>
  <form id='signature-pad-form' style='width: 100%; max-width: 480px; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 1rem;'>
    <wc-signature-pad name='signature' label='Required' required></wc-signature-pad>
    <wc-signature-pad label='Disabled' disabled></wc-signature-pad>
    <div style='display: flex; gap: 0.5rem;'>
      <wc-button type='submit'>Submit</wc-button>
      <wc-button type='reset' variant='outlined'>Reset</wc-button>
    </div>
  </form>
  <script is:inline>
    document.querySelector('#signature-pad-form').addEventListener('submit', function (event) {
      event.preventDefault();
      var file = new FormData(event.target).get('signature');
      myConsole.log('submitted ' + file.name + ', ' + file.size + ' bytes');
    });
  </script>
</DemoComponentCard>
